WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.150
Avengers: Endgame isn't just any ordinary
movie; it's the culmination of a 22-movie

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.180
saga which Iron Man kicked off 11 years ago
in 2008.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.440
And secrecy around anything for the fourth
Avengers movie has been incredibly tight,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.350
with trailers mostly showing footage from
early parts of the movie and many critics

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.820
only getting to see the finished film just
days before release.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:27.359
But that still didn't stop one of the MCU's
awesome but most spoilerific actors Mark Ruffalo

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:31.729
from accidentally revealing the end of the
movie several weeks before it hit cinemas.

00:00:31.729 --> 00:00:36.710
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm revealing how everyone's favourite Hulk,

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.190
Mark Ruffalo, let slip a massive spoiler for
Endgame during the movie's press tour.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.920
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care if
you haven't seen the film yet.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.010
With the emergence of Thanos as a seemingly
unstoppable villain in Avengers: Infinity

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:54.129
War where he snapped half of all life away,
the stakes for Avengers: Endgame grew massively.

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:59.109
So, to try and stop spoilers from leaking,
Marvel employed stricter controls than ever,

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:03.739
such as only giving partial scripts to actors
notorious for spilling spoilers and filming

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:07.250
multiple endings so they wouldn't know which
was the real one.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.640
For example, Mark Ruffalo told E! News that
he shot different endings for Endgame:

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.010
"I'm like shot five different endings to this
movie.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.010
Really?

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.830
I didn't even get a whole script to this movie.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.160
I don't know why.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.100
The script I did get had... had dummy scenes
in it."

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.530
In fact, Mark's co-star Chris Evans, who plays
Captain America, joked that Marvel didn't

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:32.810
have faith in Ruffalo's ability to stop himself
from leaking major plot points:

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:35.090
"They have to throw Mark off the scent.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.090
Why?

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.820
Because you have zero cred.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:38.820
What?!

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.070
You have earned no trust in the Marvel universe.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.070
I've like...

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.530
You leak like a bodily function.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.740
You mean, like I need a diaper?

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.740
Ah right!

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.420
Now that was good!"

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.050
The truth is that Mark does have form, with
the actor accidentally revealing the end of

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.550
Infinity War many months before the film was
released.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.910
It happened during an interview which Good
Morning America carried out with Mark and

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.530
Don Cheadle, who plays War Machine, at Disney's
D23 Expo [in 2017].

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.530
"Can I say it?

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:08.530
No!

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.979
Can I just give them a little.. a little taste?

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:13.080
I wouldn't say too much.. but you can say
as much as..

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.080
I mean, hey, it's your career.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.080
Let me just say this..

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.350
Wait till you see this next one.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.350
Ha...

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.350
Everybody dies.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.350
Dude!

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.350
Dude...!

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:21.350
Not everybody.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.350
Was that...?

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.450
Am I in trouble?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.450
A little.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.310
Is Barry gonna be mad at me?

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.310
Dude, I wouldn't...

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.310
I... just move on."

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.250
The 'Barry' Mark mentions at the end of that
clip is Barry Curtis, the head of Marvel security,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.610
who cameo-ed as the mall security guard in
Captain Marvel's movie!

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:40.700
By the way, did you notice how, just before
Mark said 'everyone dies', he sounded like

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.330
he was about to say the word 'half', which
would have been an even bigger slip given

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.900
the snap only dusted half our heroes, not
all of them!

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.200
But that wasn't the end of Mark's spoilers,
there were more to come!

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.440
In early April, many weeks before Endgame
was released at the end of the month, in his

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.740
interview with E! News, Mark went right ahead
and accidentally revealed that Chris Evans's

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.430
Captain America got married at the end of
Endgame.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.790
"Wait, is that for real, you guy's shot..?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.790
Mark's a real liability.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.790
He gets married in this!"

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.150
In the film, after the Avengers have defeated
Thanos, Steve Rogers goes on one last mission

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.550
to return the Infinity Stones to where they
were taken from in the timeline.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.640
But Steve makes a detour during his time travels
and when he returns to the present timeline,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.470
he's an old man and we discover he's now wearing
a wedding ring.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.280
And the very last scene of the movie reveals
that when Steve went back in time, he took

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.950
the opportunity to marry his long-lost love
Peggy Carter.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.290
With Chris Evans's Marvel contract finishing,
fans were theorising for months before the

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.319
release of Endgame whether the movie would
truly mark Steve Rogers' final appearance

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:45.480
as Captain America in the MCU and, if so,
whether Steve would retire or die in battle

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.849
against Thanos.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:49.959
Fortunately though, Steve got his happy ending
with Peggy.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:54.120
It's always fun to watch Mark Ruffalo during
press tours, and we're certainly big fans

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.200
of his acting in general and, of course, his
brilliant take on Bruce Banner and Hulk in

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.480
the MCU.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:04.290
But although Marvel were still under strict
lockdown when Mark accidentally revealed Cap's

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.380
final fate in Endgame weeks before the film's
release..

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.770
"He gets married in this!"
..it's worth mentioning that, at the time

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.490
of both the Endgame and Infinity War interviews,
none of us actually knew what the endings

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.269
to the movies really were.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.699
So, if you saw his Endgame interview, first
of all you might not have even taken in exactly

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:26.490
what he said, and if you did, you might still
have taken it with a pinch of salt.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.110
After all, he always seems so relaxed and
jovial that you wonder whether he's just messing

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.800
with us with his spoilers.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.060
So, revisiting his old interviews after we've
seen the movies to find out just how much

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.529
he was actually spoiling, is really just a
bit of fun!

00:04:40.529 --> 00:04:44.379
Even Marvel themselves have seen the funny
and sometimes positive side of it.

00:04:44.379 --> 00:04:50.199
Speaking to EW recently, Mark said that Marvel's
head security honcho, Barry, actually congratulated

00:04:50.199 --> 00:04:55.419
him on his genius after he accidentally live-streamed
the audio for the first 10 minutes of Thor:

00:04:55.419 --> 00:04:59.669
Ragnarok, as "[They] got more press than [they]
could have possibly paid for!"

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:04.479
And in fact, many Marvel fans love trying
to figure out spoilers and plot details by

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:09.350
analysing trailers, TV spots, toys, and other
leaks well before the movie comes out.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:14.100
But what's really interesting is the extent
to which for Avengers: Endgame, Marvel digitally

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.990
manipulated over 20 different scenes in the
trailers to avoid spoiler reveals by using

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:19.990
misdirection.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:24.270
I've actually made a video about all those
fake scenes plus other deleted scenes in Endgame

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.990
which you can tap in the top right of the
screen to watch, and there's a special Avengers

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.800
giveaway on that video.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.909
So, what do you think about Mark Ruffalo's
latest leak?

